      {
       "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "In a $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle, the side opposite $60^\\circ$ is $\\sqrt{3}$ and the hypotenuse is $2$. Therefore, $\\sin(60^\\circ)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$."
    },
    {
     "id": "21930b5a-60b9-4146-8630-4dcd70cc558c",
     "prompt": "A right-angled triangle has a $60^\\circ$ angle. The side opposite this angle is $12$ cm. What is the exact length of the adjacent side?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$4\\sqrt{3}$ cm",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$6\\sqrt{3}$ cm",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$12\\sqrt{3}$ cm",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$4$ cm",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Using $\\tan(60^\\circ)=\\sqrt{3}$ gives $\\sqrt{3}=\\frac{12}{\\text{adjacent}}$. Hence the adjacent side is $\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{3}}=4\\sqrt{3}$ cm."
    },
    {
     "id": "89222d2c-939a-44c2-8a5a-8aa9bcfcd1c4",
     "prompt": "A right-angled triangle has a $30^\\circ$ angle and a hypotenuse of $14$ cm. What is the exact length of the side opposite the $30^\\circ$ angle?",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$7\\sqrt{3}$ cm",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$7$ cm",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$14\\sqrt{3}$ cm",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$28$ cm",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Since $\\sin(30^\\circ)=\\frac{1}{2}$, the opposite side is $14\\times\\frac{1}{2}=7$ cm."
